From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] postprocess.sh: sharpen and add contrast faster

On a 20MP frame ImageMagick's -sharpen 0x1.0 -sigmoidal-contrast 6,50%
took 59 s of the 95 it takes to develop a photo on the Xperia Z1 Compact.
An unsharp mask of the same radius and amount blurs in two one-dimensional
passes where -sharpen convolves in two dimensions, and the sigmoidal curve
can be applied through a 65536-entry lookup table (-clut) instead of
computed per pixel. Together they take 35 s, and the JPEG differs from the
old one by 62 dB PSNR.

--- a/data/postprocess.sh
+++ b/data/postprocess.sh
@@ -90,7 +90,14 @@
 	if [ -n "$CONVERT" ];
 	then
 		if [ "$CONVERT" = "convert" ]; then
-			convert "$MAIN_PICTURE.$TIFF_EXT" -sharpen 0x1.0 -sigmoidal-contrast 6,50% "$TARGET_NAME.jpg"
+			# The same as -sharpen 0x1.0 -sigmoidal-contrast 6,50%, in 35 s
+			# instead of 59 on a 20MP frame on the Xperia Z1 Compact: the
+			# unsharp mask blurs in two passes where -sharpen convolves in two
+			# dimensions, and the curve goes through a lookup table instead of
+			# being computed per pixel.
+			convert "$MAIN_PICTURE.$TIFF_EXT" -unsharp 0x1+1+0 \
+				\( -size 1x65536 gradient:black-white -sigmoidal-contrast 6,50% \) -clut \
+				"$TARGET_NAME.jpg"
 		else
 			# sadly sigmoidal contrast is not available in imagemagick
 			gm convert "$MAIN_PICTURE.$TIFF_EXT" -sharpen 0x1.0 "$TARGET_NAME.jpg"
